   "subject": "Re: [poppr] poppr project",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi Dan,<div><br></div><div>We developed an open access, online primer with detailed instructions on entering data and using poppr. Please consul it at: <a href=\"https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480692461000&amp;usg=AOvVaw19gaLUj-zT-7UZOl7asACl\">https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/</a></div><div><br></div><div>Example data sets can be found int the appendix at: <a href=\"https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Data_sets.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Data_sets.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480692461000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0-nFodtIk6fylhxRbcRuTR\">https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Data_sets.html</a>. </div><div><br></div><div>Sincerely,</div><div>Nik Grunwald</div><div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Oct 9, 2017, at 8:04 PM, Dan Cooke &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">daniel...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
